+## Driving the app: Jev first
+
+```
+act on the app?
+  └─ the user said not to use Jev? ── yes ──► the verbs yourself (the loop below)
+        │ no
+        ▼
+     just puppet drive '<goal>'
+        ├─ outcome: answered    ──► read the account; query what it does not say
+        ├─ outcome: needs-agent ──► take that one step, then --resume
+        └─ outcome: take-over   ──► the verbs yourself, from where the app is
+```
+
+```bash
+just puppet drive 'In `welcome`, make the word `fox` bold, then undo it. Report line 3.'
+```
+
+Jev is the default driver: a fast decision model that takes one verb per state change, so a
+whole sequence comes back in seconds as an account of every step. `take-over` covers every
+reason it cannot drive: switched off (`FUTO_PUPPET_JEV=off`), no TypeSafe key, the service
+down, a fault, stuck twice on one goal. A user who says not to use Jev, in any words, in the
+request or in CLAUDE.md, means: skip `drive` and use the verbs. How to write a goal and read
+the account: **Delegate the driving** below.
+
+
 ## How the app is laid out
 
 Navigate it the way a person does; the verbs on offer are only what the current screen has.
